<title>CHINA: China to be long-term net copper importer - CNIEC.</title>
<headline>China to be long-term net copper importer - CNIEC.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>China will be a net copper importer in the long term because the growth of domestic output lags behind demand increases, China Non-ferrous Metals Import and Export Co (CNIEC) was quoted on Thursday as saying.</p>
<p>The China Chemical Industry News quoted CNIEC figures showing China imported 851,700 tonnes of copper in 1996, up 250,000 tonnes compared with 1995.</p>
<p>China expected an annual 13 percent growth in copper demand in the next five years, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>China has copper mine reserves of 60 million tonnes, but only half are being exploited, it said without giving further details.</p>
<p>-- Shanghai Newsroom (8621) 6279-7004</p>
</text>
